.nx
.cache
.yarn
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/plugins
# Yarn `patch:` resolutions are read during `yarn install`; the Dockerfile's
# yarn stage copies .yarn, so dropping these breaks filesystem-context builds.
!.yarn/patches
dist
reports
# The quality step builds while the image builds, so keep generated output
# out of the context: a partial apps/*/dist must never enter the image. Web
# bundles are deployed from the workflow, not from this image.
**/dist
**/reports
**/.venv
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/__pycache__
**/tmp
logs/
tmp/
coverage/
.coverage
.github/
**/*.md
docker-compose*.yml
